.TH fastrpc-healthcheck 1 "August 2026" "fastrpc" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
fastrpc\-healthcheck \- report DSP availability and FastRPC offload readiness

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fastrpc\-healthcheck
[\fB\-l\fR \fIDSP\fB:\fIPATH\fR]...
[\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fastrpc\-healthcheck
is a diagnostic utility that reports, for each Digital Signal Processor
(DSP) present on the system, whether the DSP is running and whether it is
ready to accept FastRPC offload from user space.

It gathers information from the kernel, from the DSP firmware images, and
from the FastRPC user\-space libraries, then prints a summary table. When a
DSP is not ready for offload, the reason is reported so that the missing
component can be identified.

Only Qualcomm FastRPC\-capable DSPs are examined.

.PP
Each DSP is evaluated in two stages.
.TP
.B Online
The DSP exists on the platform, its remote processor is running, and its
firmware image is present.
.TP
.B FastRPC support
An online DSP is additionally reported as supported only if the FastRPC
shell binaries are present, the FastRPC user\-space libraries are present,
the firmware and shell build IDs match, and the required FastRPC device
node exists.

.PP
A DSP being online does not by itself mean that it can be used for offload.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-lib\-path\fR \fIDSP\fB:\fIPATH\fR
Prepend \fIPATH\fR to the DSP library search path used for \fIDSP\fR.
\fIDSP\fR must be one of
.BR ADSP , CDSP , CDSP1 , GDSP0 , GDSP1 , MDSP
or
.BR SDSP .
May be given more than once, including more than once for the same DSP.
Paths given this way are searched before all others.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.

.SH OUTPUT
The report begins with the DSP firmware path, the firmware build ID of the
first DSP whose firmware and shell build IDs matched, the DSP dynamic
library path in use, and whether the system DMA\-BUF heap is available.
A value of
.B N/A
means that the item could not be determined.

.PP
One row follows per DSP found on the platform. DSPs with no
.I remoteproc
entry are omitted.
.TP
.B DSP
DSP identifier.
.TP
.B State
.B Online
or
.BR Offline .
.TP
.B SignedPD
Whether signed process domain shell binaries were found.
.TP
.B UnsignedPD
Whether unsigned process domain shell binaries were found. If unsigned
process domains are unavailable, shell binaries must be signed before they
can be run.
.TP
.B FastRPC Support
.BR Yes ,
or
.B No
followed by the first unmet requirement in parentheses, or
.B \-
if the DSP is offline.

.SH DSP LIBRARY SEARCH ORDER
DSP shell binaries are searched for in the following order. Only
directories that exist are used.
.IP 1. 4
Paths given with \fB\-\-lib\-path\fR for that DSP.
.IP 2.
The DSP\-specific subdirectory of the platform DSP library path, derived
from the machine\-specific configuration in
.IR /usr/share/qcom/conf.d/ .
.IP 3.
Directories listed in
.BR DSP_LIBRARY_PATH .
.IP 4.
The platform defaults
.I /usr/lib/dsp
and
.IR /usr/lib/rfsa/adsp .

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DSP_LIBRARY_PATH
Colon\-separated list of directories to search for DSP shell binaries, for
all DSPs.
.TP
.B LD_LIBRARY_PATH
Colon\-separated list of directories searched, in addition to
.IR /usr/lib ,
for the FastRPC user\-space libraries.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was produced. This does
.I not
indicate that any DSP is available or usable; the report itself must be
consulted.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid, or an internal error occurred.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/class/remoteproc/
DSP presence, name and running state.
.TP
.I /lib/firmware/
DSP firmware images.
.TP
.I /usr/share/qcom/conf.d/
Machine\-specific configuration giving the DSP library path. The
.I /usr/share/qcom
prefix is set at build time by the
.B \-\-with\-config\-base\-dir
configure option.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/dsp\fR, \fI/usr/lib/rfsa/adsp
Default DSP shell binary locations.
.TP
.I /dev/fastrpc\-*
FastRPC device nodes.
.TP
.I /dev/dma_heap/system
System DMA\-BUF heap, used by FastRPC for shared memory allocation.

.SH NOTES
Firmware and shell build IDs must match. A missing or mismatched build ID
always prevents FastRPC offload, and is reported as such.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fastrpc (3),
.BR dsprpcd (8)
